[size=5][b]bms-dlss – DLSS, DLAA, FSR and Frame Generation for Black Mesa[/b][/size]

Replaces Black Mesa's anti-aliasing with [b]NVIDIA DLSS / DLAA[/b] or [b]AMD FSR[/b] and adds [b]frame generation[/b] (NVIDIA DLSS Frame Generation or FSR). A much cleaner image on fences, wires and grates, and smooth high frame rates on high refresh rate monitors.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]DLAA[/b] (DLSS at native resolution) and [b]DLSS supersampling[/b] (renders larger and scales down, like DLDSR – the cleanest fences). DLSS presets K, L, M.
[*][b]AMD FSR[/b] upscaling for any graphics card with Vulkan.
[*][b]Frame Generation[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]DLSS-G[/b] (RTX 40 and newer): 2×, on [b]RTX 50 up to 6×[/b].
[*][b]FSR[/b] (any card with Vulkan – RTX 20/30, AMD, Intel): 2× and [b]3×–5×[/b] with the mod's own FSR-based generator. Not yet tested on AMD / Intel GPUs – reports welcome.
[*][b]FSR adaptive[/b]: generates only the frames that are missing to reach the target.
[*][b]Auto multiplier[/b]: the lowest multiplier that reaches your output frame rate – real frames first.
[*]Output FPS cap (default: just below your refresh rate, works with G-SYNC / FreeSync).
[/list]
[*]Motion vectors for moving objects and the weapon in hand (less ghosting).
[*]Latency reduction similar to NVIDIA Reflex when the GPU is the bottleneck.
[*]In-game menu ([b]Alt+N[/b]) in English and Czech.
[*][b]F4[/b]: experimental power saving mode (lower render resolution reconstructed by DLSS). The installer adds one line to bms\cfg\autoexec.cfg; a previous F4 binding is restored on uninstall.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Black Mesa from Steam, current Windows version. Linux / Steam Deck (Proton) is not supported.
[*]Graphics card with Vulkan. DLSS / DLAA: NVIDIA RTX. DLSS Frame Generation: RTX 40+ (more than 2×: RTX 50). FSR: any Vulkan GPU.
[*]For DLSS-G: Windows hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling on.
[*]In-game anti-aliasing (MSAA) [b]off[/b], in-game V-Sync off (use the mod's FPS cap).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Close the game.
[*]Steam > Black Mesa > Manage > Browse local files. Extract the whole zip there (a [i]bms-dlss[/i] folder appears next to bms.exe).
[*]Run [b]bms-dlss\install.bat[/b].
[*]Start the game with the Steam launch option [b]"DXVK"[/b] (Steam shows "Play DXVK"; Properties > General > Selected launch option). With "Play Black Mesa" the mod is not loaded.
[*]In game: [b]Alt+N[/b] = menu, [b]Alt+F8[/b] = mod on/off.
[/list]
After a game update or "Verify integrity of game files", run install.bat again (settings are kept). Uninstall: [b]bms-dlss\uninstall.bat[/b] (a newer DXVK from a Steam update is left unchanged).

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The mod does nothing (no Alt+N menu): start the game with the launch option "DXVK"; after a game update run install.bat again.
[*]Logs: [i]bms_dlss.log[/i] and [i]bms_dlss_helper.log[/i] in bin\thirdparty\dxvk-windows-x86. When reporting a bug, describe what you did and your GPU, and attach both logs (or use "Save a bug report" in the menu).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Frame generation: a thin halo around the weapon and hands during fast turns.
[*]DLSS-G uses the driver's own frame generation preset; NVIDIA App / Profile Inspector preset overrides may not apply.
[*]FSR 3×–5× blends very fast effects (the tau cannon beam may look doubled in generated frames).
[*]d3d9.dll and bms_dlss_helper.exe are not code-signed. The menu hotkeys use a keyboard hook limited to the game window while the game runs (not system-wide). The mod does not connect to the internet. Some antivirus programs may still warn; SHA256 checksums are included.
[*]SHA256 of bms-dlss-1.0.1.zip: 261cf67fd1b32da79aa69760566671804437912a5a1427d3f67f9ba2dfd53bf9
[*]Do not use in multiplayer.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]
[b]1.0.1[/b]
[list]
[*]Fixed: after one GPU device loss (driver reset) frame generation was turned off at every following game start.
[*]Fixed: the uninstaller could replace a newer DXVK (after a Steam update) with the old backup; running it twice is now safe.
[*]Frame generation start: longer time limit that ignores loading pauses; if it still does not start in time, it can be retried from the menu instead of staying off until a restart.
[*]Installer: works with accented characters in the Steam library path, clear error messages, a hint when install.bat is run from inside the zip, the previous F4 binding is restored on uninstall.
[*]bms_dlss.ini template in English, menu text fixes, the debug section of the menu is hidden, the menu header shows the mod version.
[*]The helper loads system libraries only from the Windows system folder.
[/list]
[b]1.0.0[/b] – first release.

